			JEST FOR KIDS 11-12-10
		Riddles and Puns for the 8 to 14 year old

			RIDDLES

Where do young dogs sleep when camping out?
    In pup tents.

How does a chocolate bar act when it tells a joke?
    It snickers.=20

How do you make a Venetian blind?
    Stick a finger in his eye.

What did the detective duck say to his partner?
    "Let's quack this case!"

When is it dangerous give a child iron supplements?
    When he goes to a magnet school.

What do you call a man sitting in a vegetable garden?
   Herb

			SCHOOL WORK

Define "Unstable" To take the horse out of the barn

Use "Semester" in a sentence: "SEMESTER whole schedule up by signing up =
for that course." (Cynthia MacGregor)

Headline: Red Tape Holds Up New Bridge

Excuses: "Please excuse Tommy for being absent yesterday. He had =
diarrhea, and his boots leak."

Country Song Title: "You Are the Apple of His Eye, But You're a Peelin' =
to Me."

			PUNS & SHORT JOKES

When my girl friend ran into an old flame, it burned me up.

"Doctor, please help me! An alligator bit off my foot!" "Which one?" =
"How should I know? All these gators look alike to me."

The tailor was fired because he didn't measure up.=20

I know of a man who spent his entire adult life collecting memorabilia =
about Wonder Woman, Joan of Arc and Florence Nightingale. Apparently, he =
was a heroine addict! (Gary Hallock)

Whether it's a pancake or a baseball team, the secret is to start with a =
good batter.

			GROANERS & LONG JOKES

      I think that I shall never see
      A billboard lovely as a tree.
      Perhaps, unless the billboards fall,
      I'll never see a tree at all.
             (Ogden Nash)

I was walking across campus with my friend, Doug when he pointed up at a =
large bird overhead and said, "Look, it's an eagle!" "That doesn't look =
like it's an eagle," I remarked. "Well of course not," he shot back, =
"It's travelling incognito. Don't you know that eagles are masters of de =
skys?"

A friend of mine used to work at the local animal shelter. They looked =
after all kinds of sick, injured and abandoned animals. One day a rabbit =
was brought in with rabies. Other than the fact that it was always =
running around very fast, it had the most pleasant personality. My =
friend fell in love with it. She decided to take the rabbit home and =
care for it. Time passed and every time a rabbit with rabies was brought =
into the shelter she would take it home. To this day she has cared for =
hundreds of these rabbits. She has a rapid rabid rabbit habit.


